aking a position here on that  that's a debate in and of itself about  what makes sense and what doesn't make  sense  protectionism America economic  nationalism etc but they said this was  one of the things they wanted to deal  with and they are not dealing with it in  phase one of this deal it also does not  end the trade war it does not remove the  disastrous tariffs now of course the  Trump administration says all of that is  going to come in phase two so really the  headline here is something has been  passed Donald Trump can claim it as a  win people who don't know much  believe that it's a win and maybe when  you go interview Trump supporters at  rallies and say what is Trump accomplish  that you like they'll say well he did  the phase one trade deal even if in  reality it doesn't do very much now to  be charitable if I wanted to be as  charitable as possible about this phase  one deal I could say signing something  anything as long as it has even a tiny  step forward it could generate momentum  for doing something bigger okay I mean  that's the most charitable analysis and  time will tell whether it's a good  analysis whether it actually leads to  anything further but again it's just an  opportunity for Trump to brag and here  he is doing it the agreement tears down  major market barriers for us food and  agricultural exports China will now  welcome American beef and pork poultry  seafood rice dairy infant formula animal  feed biotechnology and much much more so  you get the idea now let me talk a  little bit about the trade imbalance  this is really important to understand  and I I've mentioned it in passing  before Donald Trump constantly talks  about the trade deficit we're importing  way more from China than we are  exporting to China and we've got to fix  this you don't just fix that because our  economy for decades has been based on  that decades ago when outsourcing of  labor started to go elsewhere  when outsourcing of manufacturing  started to go el